.TH UGREEN-LED-TOOLS 1 "2026-11-09" "UGREEN LED controller" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ugreen-blink-disk, ugreen-check-standby, ugreen-detect-disks, ugreen-detect-network, ugreen-diskiomon, ugreen-netdevmon, ugreen-netdevmon-multi, ugreen-power-led, ugreen-probe-leds \- configure and monitor UGREEN NAS LEDs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ugreen-probe-leds
.br
.B ugreen-detect-disks
.RI [ ata | hctl | serial ]
.br
.B ugreen-detect-network
.br
.B ugreen-diskiomon
.br
.B ugreen-netdevmon
.I interface
.br
.B ugreen-netdevmon-multi
.br
.B ugreen-power-led
.br
.B ugreen-blink-disk
.I interval device led
.RI [ device " " led ...]
.br
.B ugreen-check-standby
.I interval standby-color normal-colors device led
.RI [ device " " led ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
These tools require compatible UGREEN hardware. Run LED setup and monitoring
as root. Configuration is read from /etc/ugreen-leds.conf.
.PP
ugreen-probe-leds loads the driver and registers the LED controller on the
Intel I801 SMBus. It requires the DKMS module and matching kernel headers.
.PP
ugreen-diskiomon monitors disk activity, standby and optional health state.
Verify physical disk-slot mapping before relying on its LED indications.
.PP
ugreen-netdevmon uses the kernel netdev trigger for one interface.
ugreen-netdevmon-multi aggregates RX/TX counters for selected or all physical
Ethernet interfaces. Run only one network monitor at a time.
.PP
ugreen-power-led applies the configured power LED appearance. The detection
tools print suggested disk mappings and available network interfaces.
.PP
ugreen-blink-disk and ugreen-check-standby are helpers normally started by
ugreen-diskiomon. Intervals are in seconds. Devices are block-device basenames
such as sda; LEDs are names such as disk1. Colors are quoted RGB triples;
normal-colors is a comma-separated list of triples, one for each device.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ugreen-leds.conf
Administrator configuration, preserved by dpkg.
.TP
.I /etc/ugreen-leds/network.conf
Initial Debian network selections. Settings in the main configuration override
these selections. NETWORK_MODE is single, multi or all; NETWORK_INTERFACES is
a space-separated list. NETDEV_BLINK_RX and NETDEV_BLINK_TX control activity
sampling. NETDEV_POLL_INTERVAL defaults to 0.1 seconds.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ugreen_leds_cli (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR dkms (8)
